/target
**/*.rs.bk

# Local lifecycle state, logs, process ownership locks, and the pinned-tool caches: the `lyracore`
# CLI (.lyracore/cli/<rev>/) and the wire harness (.lyracore/wire-harness/<sha>/, #246 — a checkout
# of LyraCoreProject/wire-harness plus its own target/, which is why this must stay ignored).
/.lyracore/

# Operator-pulled third-party data (cmangos classic-db) + generated bundles — NEVER committed (licensing firewall)
/.import/

# Blizzard client data — extracted DBCs / MPQ archives are COPYRIGHTED and MUST NEVER be committed.
# The importer parses the operator's own client MPQs IN MEMORY and emits only derived game_* values;
# this is a backstop in case a stray extract is ever written to the tree (the code never writes one).
**/*.dbc
**/*.MPQ
**/*.mpq
DBFilesClient/

# Runtime logs (gateway/wine stderr captured by the wow-mcp harness) — never committed.
gateway/gateway-stderr.log
*-stderr.log

# Stray `cargo doc` output at repo root.
/doc/

# Heap-profiling output from the `dhat-heap` feature (work-item 292, Runbook C).
dhat-heap.json
__pycache__/

# cargo-mutants report output (#380). Regenerated on every run; the CI job uploads it as an
# artifact instead. `.cargo/mutants.toml` is the configuration and IS checked in.
/mutants.out/
/mutants.out.old/
.scratch/

# Agent-created Git worktrees are local execution state, not repository content.
/.claude/worktrees/

# Local fan-out briefs are agent execution state, not repository content.
/.claude/tickets/

# The Datascript toolchain's Bun project. `package.json`, `bun.lock`, `tsconfig.json` and the
# Datascripts under `src/` ARE committed — the pin and the code are repository content.
#
# `generated/` is not: it is a ~400-file, 2 MB projection of the Module wasm that
# `lyracore packages build` reproduces from `spacetime generate --lang typescript` on every run.
# Committing it would put a large mechanical diff in every schema change and, worse, create a
# second source of truth that can disagree with the Module. The Module is the schema's authority.
#
# `generated/base-snapshot.json` rides the same rule for a second reason: the importer derives it
# from the OPERATOR's own client data (`--spell-snapshot`). It carries only mapped `game_*` values,
# never client bytes, but it is the operator's own derived data and stays on the operator's machine.
/datascripts/generated/
/datascripts/node_modules/

# Packages installed on a host (`lyracore packages add`) are local to that checkout. Unknown
# Package directories stay out of Git status. New files and generated artifacts in the committed
# first-party Packages remain visible.
/packages/*
!/packages/blackfathom_deeps/
!/packages/blackrock_depths/
!/packages/dire_maul/
!/packages/eventai_instance_test/
!/packages/example/
!/packages/fire_nova/
!/packages/razorfen_kraul/
!/packages/shadowfang_keep/
!/packages/sunken_temple/
!/packages/wailing_caverns/
!/packages/zulgurub/
